## 4. Conflicting and unverified information

This section separates unresolved evidence from established findings. Conflicting reports must not be presented as confirmed facts.

{% set has_disputes = namespace(value=false) %}
{% for s in r.subjects %}
  {% if s.disputed %}
    {% set has_disputes.value = true %}
### {{ s.name | esc }}{% if s.role %} — {{ s.role | esc }}{% endif %}

{% for f in s.disputed %}
{{ finding(f) | trim }}

{% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if not has_disputes.value %}
No explicitly disputed findings were recorded by the workflow.
{% endif %}

{% set has_unverified = namespace(value=false) %}
{% for s in r.subjects %}
  {% for f in s.findings %}
    {% if f.verification == "SINGLE_SOURCE" %}
      {% set has_unverified.value = true %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

{% if has_unverified.value %}
**Verification limitation:** Some reportable claims rely on a single source. They should be treated as leads for further verification, not as independently established facts.
{% endif %}

